1
00:00:03,202 --> 00:00:06,708
Supplier bank-detail fraud starts with one email asking a

2
00:00:06,708 --> 00:00:09,352
clerk to change where a supplier gets paid.

3
00:00:09,802 --> 00:00:12,616
Here every change rises through a lock

4
00:00:12,616 --> 00:00:16,912
flight: request, call-back, second approval, then release.

5
00:00:18,011 --> 00:00:21,870
Each boat is a change request in the chamber of the gate

6
00:00:21,870 --> 00:00:26,281
it has reached; pennants are red flags, and this one flies four.

7
00:00:27,087 --> 00:00:29,649
Switch the lens to flags and every hull

8
00:00:29,649 --> 00:00:32,277
is painted by how many flags it carries.

9
00:00:33,078 --> 00:00:37,488
Today ranks what needs attention: the four-flag change, one account

10
00:00:37,488 --> 00:00:41,108
shared by two suppliers, and a call-back still waiting.

11
00:00:41,558 --> 00:00:44,758
Choosing an item flies me to the boat behind it.

12
00:00:45,566 --> 00:00:48,997
A domestic payment run is due tomorrow, so the second key

13
00:00:48,997 --> 00:00:52,066
is frozen, and the sign says exactly when it opens.

14
00:00:52,879 --> 00:00:57,029
View as a clerk, and only the call-backs waiting on me stay lit.

15
00:00:59,585 --> 00:01:02,895
The call-back screen shows only the number already

16
00:01:02,895 --> 00:01:05,345
on file, never the one in the letter.

17
00:01:05,795 --> 00:01:08,858
Dial the number from the letter instead, and the app

18
00:01:08,858 --> 00:01:11,745
says plainly that this call cannot open the gate.

19
00:01:12,549 --> 00:01:16,999
Sam raised the Lindqvist change, so the second key refuses him.

20
00:01:17,799 --> 00:01:22,269
Jordan, the finance controller, sees every flag with its reason,

21
00:01:22,269 --> 00:01:26,389
including the account already on file for another supplier.

22
00:01:26,839 --> 00:01:30,164
With four flags up, approving needs a written

23
00:01:30,164 --> 00:01:33,489
override reason, and it goes into the ledger.

24
00:01:34,295 --> 00:01:36,787
The second key turns, the gate opens, and

25
00:01:36,787 --> 00:01:39,035
the boat rises into the next chamber.

26
00:01:41,350 --> 00:01:44,371
A known number, a second person, a freeze before

27
00:01:44,371 --> 00:01:47,770
every run, and no full account number stored anywhere.
